{"item_id": "feed:https://www.ssusa.org/content/new-mdt-one-piece-night-vision-bridge/", "version_id": "154009e503ea72f9f4e7321c04b365252bf5f2676aa1be831c7241f65755f7d4", "decision": "reject", "reason": "The item is an NRA-published product post for an MDT one-piece night vision bridge, which is a rail/mount in scope under shooting support and spotting gear, but the source notes flag it as a manufacturer-close press release with only manufacturer specs, price, and compatibility claims, and no independent testing or practitioner use is reported, so it does not meet the Credibility and Commercial incentives standards for acceptance. Its 'Mostly firearm content' framing and the rule that manufacturer performance claims need independent support mean it is best deferred rather than accepted; under the policy's Making-the-decision rules, a relevant item with evidence too thin to rely on should be deferred, so I'm correcting this to defer.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://bulletin.accurateshooter.com/2026/10/how-to-find-your-scopes-true-click-values-with-box-test/", "version_id": "7a62836f185d8550938253297ef501eee2aac8e2783e7d4fa09298e86af41728", "decision": "accept", "reason": "Under Relevance and Credibility, this item addresses riflescope click verification, a spotting and measuring gear topic, and reports a reader's measured test (a Leupold 6.5-20X50 M1 reading about 5% off true MOA) plus a Bryan Litz comment, which counts as practitioner testing rather than restated specs. Its central claim rests on a single reader's test and an expert quote, so it is attributed rather than presented as established fact, and Litz's commentary on ballistic error is noted as an opinion. Best supports Piece 02 (What holds up?) because it tests a manufacturer's advertised click values against field measurement.", "piece_ids": ["02"]}
{"item_id": "feed:https://bulletin.accurateshooter.com/2026/10/breathing-control-can-help-you-see-better-and-shoot-better/", "version_id": "c142a703795fe7e94e4cca1bc9865915fe72fb8ea63fc4f0eb83cb85d5fbc956", "decision": "reject", "reason": "This is a forum-derived shooting technique and eye-fatigue discussion with no gear evaluation, so it falls outside the Relevance categories and the policy's focus on gear that Mammoth competitors would carry. Anecdotal forum advice about breathing and vision does not support a gear claim, so it does not meet the Credibility standard for acceptance either.", "piece_ids": []}
